<article class="env-lemma" id="005J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/005J">Lemma <span data-tag="005J">5.15.4</span>.</a> Let $U \subset X$ be open. For a constructible set $E \subset X$ the intersection $E \cap U$ is constructible in $U$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $V \subset X$ is retrocompact open in $X$. It suffices to show that $V \cap U$ is retrocompact in $U$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/005I" data-tag="005I">5.15.3</a>. To show this let $W \subset U$ be open and quasi-compact. Then $W$ is open and quasi-compact in $X$. Hence $V \cap W = V \cap U \cap W$ is quasi-compact as $V$ is retrocompact in $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>